
 filloneorder - Add a single ad-hoc order record to the 'ousage' table.

 Inserts one order/usage row into the 'ousage' table in PostgreSQL
 database 'rdadb'. Use this when an order needs to be recorded manually
 outside the normal automated pipelines.

 USAGE:
   filloneorder -e UserEmail -m DeliveryMethod -t DatasetID -v DataVolume
                [-a CostAmount] [-b] [-c FileCount] [-d DateOrdered]
                [-i InputDataVolume] [-o OrderID] [-p PaymentMethod]
                [-s SpecialistLoginName]
                [-x DateClosed [TimeClosed]]

 REQUIRED OPTIONS:

   -e UserEmail            Email address of the user who placed the order.
   -m DeliveryMethod       Delivery method for the ordered data.
   -t DatasetID            Dataset the data was ordered from.
   -v DataVolume           Final delivered data volume.

 OPTIONAL OPTIONS:

   -a CostAmount           Order cost in dollars (omit for free orders).
   -c FileCount            Number of data files in the order.
   -d DateOrdered          Date the order was opened.
   -i InputDataVolume      Input data volume processed for the order.
   -o OrderID              Order ID, up to 30 characters.
   -p PaymentMethod        Payment method matching the -a amount.
   -s SpecialistLoginName  Specialist who handled the order. Defaults to
                           the current user; if invalid, defaults to the
                           dataset owner.
   -x DateClosed [TimeClosed]
                           Date (and optional time) the order was closed.
   -b                      Run in background mode (log to file only).

 EXAMPLE:
   filloneorder -e user@example.com -m FTP -t d540001 -v 1500 \
                -c 25 -d 2024-01-15 -o ORDER12345
